Project Title

House Price Prediction Using Linear Regression

Objective

The objective of this project is to build a machine learning model that predicts house prices based on various property features. Linear Regression is used to train the model and evaluate its performance. The project helps understand how different features influence house prices and enables data-driven price estimation.

Dataset

The dataset contains housing information including:

Property area
Number of bedrooms and bathrooms
Furnishing status
Location details
Amenities (air conditioning, parking, etc.)
House price (target variable)

Tools and Libraries Used
Python
Pandas
NumPy
Matplotlib
Seaborn
Scikit-learn
Jupyter Notebook

Steps Performed
1. Data Loading
Imported the housing dataset (Housing.csv) using Pandas.
2. Data Inspection
Viewed first few rows using head()
Checked data types and structure using info()
Reviewed statistical summary using describe()
3. Data Preprocessing
Checked for missing values
Converted categorical columns into numerical form using One-Hot Encoding (pd.get_dummies)
4. Feature Selection
Defined feature matrix X by dropping the target column (price)
Defined target vector y as the price column
5. Train-Test Split
Split the dataset into 80% training data and 20% testing data using train_test_split with random_state=42
6. Model Building
Created a Linear Regression model using Scikit-learn
Trained the model on the training dataset
Generated predictions on the test dataset
7. Model Evaluation

Evaluated the model using:

Mean Squared Error (MSE)
R-Squared Score (R²)
8. Feature Importance
Extracted model coefficients to understand the impact of each feature on house price prediction.
9. Data Visualization

Created:

Scatter Plot — Actual vs. Predicted house prices
Line Plot — Comparison of actual and predicted price values

Key Insights
The Linear Regression model successfully learned the relationship between house features and prices.
Feature importance (coefficients) revealed which property attributes most strongly influence price.
The scatter plot of actual vs. predicted prices showed how closely the model predictions aligned with real values.
R² Score indicated the proportion of variance in house prices explained by the model.

Outcome

This project improved understanding of:

Data preprocessing and encoding techniques
Supervised machine learning using Linear Regression
Model evaluation using MSE and R² Score
Feature importance analysis
Data visualization for model performance

Conclusion

The project successfully built a house price prediction model using Linear Regression. The model provided meaningful predictions based on property features and demonstrated how machine learning can be applied to real estate data for price estimation and business decision-making.
